{"workflow_id":"pw_1058be43f6482ca64fa86b7d","name":"Statsmodels question digest","status":"confirmed","source":"pondflow","revision":3,"solution_id":"statsmodels-question-digest","solution_version":"1.0.0","entry_workflow_key":"setup-watch","workflow_keys":["setup-watch","morning-digest"],"agent_keys":["digest"],"filename":"statsmodels-question-digest-1.0.0.pas","package_base64":"","package_sha256":"sha256:271f0e59da995c44f9fadbe670a4bf3b4a1ade9bf718a965b0a39e1104881cb7","package_bytes":99828,"entry_workflow_markdown":"# Set up the watches\n\n## Trigger\nManual: the first run after \"go\", or \"restart the watches\" in chat.\n\n## Preconditions\n- Intake facts known (`resources/run-card.md`).\n- Run log created at `statsmodels-digest/runs/\u003cdate\u003e-\u003cn\u003e.md`.\n\n## Stages\n1. Check existing watches. Owner: digest. Tool: `pond_watch_list` with `label` statsmodels-digest, `status` all. Second source: none (manages a watch). Budget: 1 call. Errors: common. Log: watches found with status and days left. Passes: which of the three watches are missing, expired or stopped.\n2. Confirm scrapers. Owner: digest. Tool: `pond_scraper_list` (no arguments). Second source: none (no data is read). Budget: 1 call. Errors: common; a scraper not returned → mark that source `[NEED: Pond \u003cscraper\u003e]` and carry it on the web source in the digest. Log: `reddit` and `hacker_news_stories` listed or not. Passes: the starts to propose.\n3. Approval gate. See below.\n4. Start watches. Owner: digest. Tool: `pond_scrape_start`, one call per approved start, each with `label` statsmodels-digest and `repeat` daily: (a) `scraper` reddit, `queries` [\"statsmodels\", \"quantile regression python\"]; (b) `scraper` hacker_news_stories, `query` \"statsmodels\"; (c) `scraper` hacker_news_stories, `query` \"quantile regression\". An expired or stopped watch is restarted with `pond_watch_extend` and its `watch_id` instead. Second source: none (starts a watch). Budget: 3 starts or extends. Errors: common; `too_many_watches` → stop, show the member their watches and ask which to stop; `plan_changed` on extend → propose a new start. Log: each `watch_id` and `run_id`. Passes: watch ids.\n5. First results. Owner: digest. Tool: `pond_scrape_status` with each `run_id`, every 15 seconds for at most 10 minutes. Second source: none (the digest reads the posts). Budget: 40 polls per run in total. Errors: common; `failed` or `skipped_budget` → report it neutrally and continue with the others. Log: status and items per watch. Passes: `dataset_id` per watch to Morning digest, which then runs once.\n\n## Approval gate\nBefore any watch is started or extended: show the three starts (Reddit search for the two topics; Hacker News \"statsmodels\"; Hacker News \"quantile regression\"), that each runs once now and daily for 7 days, and the budget of 3 starts. The member approves the starts by name; an unapproved start is not made.\n\n## Side effects\nNone until approval. After approval: up to three Pond watches labelled `statsmodels-digest`.\n\n## Evidence and logging\nEach start is logged with its `watch_id`, `run_id` and status. Run log per the run card.\n\n## Failure policy\n`manual-review`: on an error not listed above, log it, say which watch is not running, and ask the member how to proceed.\n\n## Completion criteria\nEvery approved watch has a `watch_id` and a first run that is `succeeded`, or is reported with its reason; the `finished` line is in the run log.\n","display_graph":{"groups":[{"id":"collect","label":"Collect"},{"id":"pick","label":"Pick"},{"id":"deliver","label":"Deliver"}],"nodes":[{"id":"morning","type":"trigger","group":"collect","title":"Weekday 8am","summary":"Starts every weekday at 08:00 Los Angeles time, or when you ask.","kind":"trigger","pas_ref":"workflows/morning-digest"},{"id":"watching","type":"condition","group":"collect","title":"Watches running?","summary":"Checks that the Reddit and Hacker News watches are still collecting.","ports":["yes","no"],"pas_ref":"workflows/morning-digest"},{"id":"approve-watch","type":"approval","group":"collect","title":"You approve the watches","summary":"You say yes before any watch is started or kept alive.","pas_ref":"workflows/setup-watch"},{"id":"start-watch","type":"action","group":"collect","title":"Start watching","summary":"Starts the Reddit and Hacker News watches for the two topics.","kind":"source","source_ids":["reddit","hackernews"],"pas_ref":"workflows/setup-watch"},{"id":"read-posts","type":"step","group":"collect","title":"Read new posts","summary":"Reads posts from the last 3 days that mention statsmodels or quantile regression.","kind":"source","source_ids":["reddit","hackernews","pond"],"pas_ref":"workflows/morning-digest"},{"id":"in-scope","type":"step","group":"pick","title":"Keep what is in scope","summary":"Keeps the four subreddits and Hacker News, drops job posts, old posts and repeats.","kind":"filter","pas_ref":"workflows/morning-digest"},{"id":"flag","type":"step","group":"pick","title":"Flag unanswered questions","summary":"Marks the posts that ask a question nobody has answered yet.","kind":"ai","pas_ref":"agents/digest"},{"id":"digest","type":"action","group":"deliver","title":"Digest in chat","summary":"Sends up to 10 posts with title, link, source and a one-line summary.","kind":"output","pas_ref":"workflows/morning-digest"},{"id":"done","type":"end","title":"Done","summary":"Run complete."}],"edges":[{"from":"morning","to":"watching"},{"from":"watching","from_port":"yes","to":"read-posts","label":"Running"},{"from":"watching","from_port":"no","to":"approve-watch","label":"Not running"},{"from":"approve-watch","to":"start-watch"},{"from":"start-watch","to":"read-posts"},{"from":"read-posts","to":"in-scope"},{"from":"in-scope","to":"flag"},{"from":"flag","to":"digest"},{"from":"digest","to":"done"}]},"run_guidance":"How Grok Bot should pull and run this PondFlow workflow:\n\n1. Call pond_workflow_export with the workflow_id (confirmed preferred; draft also works).\n2. Decode package_base64 and write statsmodels-question-digest-1.0.0.pas under the Bot workspace (verify package_sha256).\n3. Unpack the .pas ZIP (pas.json + agents/ + workflows/ + tests/).\n4. Create or update local Agents from agents/*/AGENT.md.\n5. Follow workflows/setup-watch/WORKFLOW.md step by step. Pause at every display_graph node with type \"approval\".\n6. Use Pond MCP tools only when the workflow text or connectors name them (for example pond_web_search). Never send or mutate externally without owner approval.\n7. Optional later: if/when Pond publishes customer packs to the catalog, switch to pas_install_* — today that path is unavailable for solution id statsmodels-question-digest.\n8. Do not call pond_pas_routine_activation_* unless a routine was installed locally and the owner explicitly asked to activate it.","catalog_install_note":"Customer-authored PondFlow exports are not in the Pond PAS catalog. Do not call pas_catalog_search, pas_package_inspect, or pas_install_* for this pack. Unpack package_base64 locally and run from the markdown + display_graph approval gates."}
